-- title:
--   Reduced norms of away-from-v units are ± powers of r
-- statement:
--   Fix rationals $a,b$ and let $R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is an order in the sense of the predicate `IsOrder`: $1\in R$, $R$ is closed under multiplication, the $\mathbb{Q}$-span of $R$ is all of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, and $R$ is finitely generated as a $\mathbb{Z}$-module. Let $r$ be a prime natural number and $v$ a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that the image of $r$ in $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in the prime ideal $v$. Let $\gamma$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ belonging to `awayUnits R v`, the subgroup obtained as the infimum, over all height-one primes $w\neq v$, of the preimages under the map `toLoc w` (induced on units by $x\mapsto x\otimes 1$ into $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w$) of the subgroup generated by [`Submodule.localBoxUnits R w`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L45), the set of units of the completed algebra lying, together with their inverses, in the local box of $R$ at $w$. The conclusion is that there exist natural numbers $i,j$ with $\mathrm{nrd}(\gamma)\cdot r^{i}=r^{j}$ or $\mathrm{nrd}(\gamma)\cdot r^{i}=-r^{j}$, where $\mathrm{nrd}(x)=x_{\mathrm{re}}^{2}-a\,x_{I}^{2}-b\,x_{J}^{2}+ab\,x_{K}^{2}$.
--
--   This records that the reduced norm of a unit which is locally integral and invertible away from $v$ is a unit of $\mathbb{Z}[1/r]$, i.e. $\pm r^{k}$ for some $k\in\mathbb{Z}$, written here in the cleared form $\mathrm{nrd}(\gamma)r^{i}=\pm r^{j}$. It is used in the construction of the coset graph attached to a definite quaternion algebra in the Cerednik–Drinfeld setting, in the identification of the conjugation action on away units and in the dictionary between isogeny pairs of fake elliptic curves and quaternionic endomorphisms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_CosetGraph_exists_nrd_mul_pow_eq_pow_of_mem_awayUnits.lean

